cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use holo in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "holo: holographic computing on FHRR hypervectors"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Squatch CC"
license: FSL-1.1-Apache-2.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22116367
repository-code: "https://github.com/squatch-stack/hdc-holo"
abstract: >-
  Holographic data structures, Gaussian-splat scene fields, ridge-fitted
  holograms, closed-form X-ray rendering, and CRDT replication with
  observed-remove deletion, all on one substrate: bundles of complex64
  FHRR phasors. Includes measured capacity laws, tagged wire/storage
  formats, a real-capture pipeline (.splat/.spz), and an MLX/Metal
  backend with a NumPy fallback.
keywords:
  - hyperdimensional computing
  - vector symbolic architectures
  - holographic reduced representations
  - gaussian splatting
  - random fourier features
  - CRDT
